      "nets": ["NET0175", "Net-(U55-Y)", "Net-(U40-A)", "NET0132", "NET0185", "NET0213", "NET0160"],
      "observed": "These parts are specified by their value as SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1, but their sourcing fields list MPN U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R and LCSC C171458. The 1G125 is a tri-state push-pull buffer, whereas the intended 1G07 is an open-drain buffer. The mismatch is repeated across the buffer instances.",
      "expected": "The sourced parts should be open-drain SN74LVC1G07-compatible buffers, consistent with the schematic value and the specification's use of 1G07 parts as sink/buffer elements.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U8\") (value \"SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(field (name \"MPN\") \"U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(field (name \"LCSC\") \"C171458\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "an e-stop loop ... gated through single non-inverting buffers (SN74LVC1G07, parts U15, U22, U35, U36) wired as /OE-controlled sinks"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the BOM/sourcing fields determine the fitted parts, the push-pull outputs can actively drive high where the intended open-drain outputs only sink or release the line. That can break wired sink behavior and cause contention or incorrect signaling in circuits using these buffers, including safety-related sink paths.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic values call for open-drain SN74LVC1G07 buffers, but the repeated sourcing fields identify tri-state U74LVC1G125 parts instead. If assembled from those sourcing fields, the outputs will not have the intended open-drain behavior."
}

